blocks.en:
Building on L1, this level assesses the model’s ability to integrate evidence across charts and reason about changes and relationships over time ( Amini et al., 2015 ; Thompson et al., 2020 ; Hao et al., 2024 ) .
It contains four question types: Cross-Temporal Change , tracking how events evolve and extrapolate over time; Cross-Chart Comparison , comparing values across charts or deriving, through arithmetic, results not stated explicitly in the video ( Cleveland and McGill, 1984 ) ; Causal Reasoning , identifying causal chains supported by evidence from multiple charts;
and Argument Synthesis , identifying the key evidence that supports the video’s central argument.

blocks.zh:
